```

In this example, Fibonacci is the class that implements the algorithm to find the closest Fibonacci numbers.

The first test case checks whether the algorithm works correctly for negative input values. It expects the closest Fibonacci number to be 0 and the next one to be 1.

The second test case checks whether the algorithm works correctly for large input values. It expects the closest Fibonacci number to be 832040 and the next one to be 1346269.

public static class Fibonacci
{
    public static (int closest, int next) GetClosestFibonacciNumbers(double number)
    {
        if (number < 0)
        {
            return (0, 1);
        }

        int previous = 0;
        int current = 1;

        while (true)
        {
            int nextFibonacci = previous + current;

            if (nextFibonacci > number)
            {
                return (current, nextFibonacci);
            }

            previous = current;
            current = nextFibonacci;
        }
    }
}

